<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φείδων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>oil-can with a narrow neck, that lets only a little run
				out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.179
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as pr.n.
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φείδων</span></b> , king of Argos,
			the author of Peloponnesian weights and measures, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.127
			</span></i>:— hence Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φειδώνειος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φειδώνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, μέτρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					10.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				480
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				30.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.3.33
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
			</span></i> l. c. connects signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> with the Adj.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέδιμνοι Φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Delph.</u>
					3(5).3
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				 ii 3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> name of an old man in Com., <i>Thrifty,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				191.21
			</span></i>, etc.:—hence Com. patron. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φειδωνίδης</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i>Thrifty-son,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				65
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
